DISCOVERED gap (all modes), NOT the qualified-type overlay: a cross-package generic interface with a LIBRARY-SIDE impl can't be upcast at the consumer. main upcasts `&m` (an iflib.IntImpl) to `*iflib.Box[int]` where `impl IntImpl : Box[int]` lives in iflib — the consumer can't find/wire iflib's vtable for the (IntImpl, Box[int]) instantiation, so the interface value is nil/unwired: VM reports "call through nil interface value", native produces no output. The MANAGED form (`@Box[int]`) instead emits `extractvalue operand must be aggregate type`. Confirmed library-side-impl is the trigger (reproduces with an iflib-LOCAL struct result too, not just the qualified dep.Tag) — 464 works because its impl is consumer-side. Independent of the d2a9ff20/83971b2e qualified-import fix. This test uses a qualified method result (dep.Tag) so that, once the upcast/vtable gap is fixed, it ALSO covers the generic-interface qualified-method-type overlay (the currently-uncovered interface counterpart of conformance 841/850/853). Want: 15. See claude-todo.md.
